%SIXMD 1
# @?MOUNTALL - APPLY CONFIGURED FILESYSTEM MOUNTS

## DESCRIPTION

MOUNTALL IS AN INIT HELPER THAT READS /CONFIG/FSTAB AND MOUNTS THE
FILESYSTEMS LISTED THERE.  IT DOES NOT DISCOVER OR FORMAT MEDIA.

USAGE IS 'MOUNTALL'.  THE CONFIGURATION FILE MUST BE PRESENT.
PROCESSING STOPS AT THE FIRST INVALID ENTRY OR FAILED MOUNT.
BLANK LINES AND COMMENT LINES BEGINNING WITH '#' ARE IGNORED.

## @?FILES

### @?/CONFIG/FSTAB
ONE MOUNT PER LINE.  CURRENTLY SUPPORTED FORMS ARE
'MEMFS:/MOUNTPOINT:WORDS[:PERSIST]' AND
'DTFS:/DEV/DTCN:/MOUNTPOINT:RW'.  MOUNT POINTS MUST EXIST.
MEMFS IS A SINGLETON; PERSIST REQUESTS PERSISTENT MEMFS POLICY.
THE DTFS FORM REQUESTS THE NATIVE WRITABLE TAPE PERSONALITY.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - ALL REQUESTED MOUNTS SUCCEEDED
### @?1 - INVALID ENTRY OR MOUNT FAILURE
### @?2 - CONFIGURATION FILE COULD NOT BE OPENED

